# Build-context exclusions for deploy/Dockerfile.
#
# READ THIS BEFORE RELYING ON IT — measured 2026-08-03, docker 29.5.2, classic
# builder (no buildx on this machine):
#
#   docker build -f deploy/Dockerfile ... <repo root>
#
# reads ONLY <context>/.dockerignore. A file at deploy/.dockerignore is NOT
# consulted. Both legs were run with identical bytes: at deploy/ the excluded
# directory landed in the image; at the context root it did not.
#
# So this file is documentation of intent, not an enforced control. The image is
# kept clean structurally instead: deploy/Dockerfile enumerates its COPY lines
# rather than using `COPY . /app`, and strips bytecode afterwards. To make these
# patterns actually shrink the build context, copy this file to the repo root as
# .dockerignore.
#
# Patterns are matched against the path relative to the context root and are not
# recursive unless prefixed with **/ — hence the **/ forms below.
# Kept consistent with .gitignore (byte-compiled files, .venv, caches,
# findings/).

.git
.git/**
.venv
findings/
__pycache__
**/__pycache__
*.pyc
**/*.pyc
*.pyo
**/*.pyo
.pytest_cache
**/.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
**/.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
**/.ruff_cache
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.env
